    <div>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">How this was determined</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        <p>Each individual participant involved in the effort was allowed to select which non-profit he or she would prefer to send the prize money. Each person was given one vote per RC5-64 block submitted. The non-profit that receives the most votes was given 60% of the prize money.</p>
        <p>For RC5-64, participants voted for distributed.net, itself, to be the non-profit that would receive the 60% of the money.</p>
        <p>Of the remaining 40%, 10% was given to the individual who found the key and 10% was given to that person's team. Since the winning individual was NOT on a team when they found the key, they received the entire 20%.</p>
        <p>The 20% remaining was given to the runner-up non-profit as determined by the participant voting.</p>
        <p>Is everyone confused yet?</p>
      </div>
