    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
      <div class="phead2 bg-slate-100 py-2 text-center">Non-Profit Information and Links</div>
      <div class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
        <div class="p-3">
          <a class="font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" href="http://www.cpsr.org">CPSR</a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">CPSR is a public-interest alliance of computer scientists and others concerned about the impact of computer technology on society. We work to influence decisions regarding the development and use of computers because those decisions have far-reaching consequences and reflect our basic values and priorities.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3">
          <a class="font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" href="http://www.epic.org/">EPIC</a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">EPIC is a public interest research center in Washington, D.C. It was established in 1994 to focus public attention on emerging civil liberties issues and to protect privacy, the First Amendment, and constitutional values. EPIC is a project of the Fund for Constitutional Government. EPIC works in association with Privacy International, an international human rights group based in London, UK and is also a member of the Global Internet Liberty Campaign, the Internet Free Expression Alliance and the Internet Privacy Coalition.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3">
          <a class="font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" href="http://www.debian.org/donations.html">Software in the Public Interest</a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">Software in the Public Interest is a non-profit corporation formed by the developers of the Debian Linux Distribution. Their goal is to promote and distribute free software. You can read about their approach in the Debian Social Contract, at <a class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" href="http://www.debian.org/social_contract.html">http://www.debian.org/social_contract.html</a>. Since its incorporation SPI has expanded to include the Open Hardware Certification program and the Berlin project. They provided resources and money grants to other free software projects such as GNOME.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3">
          <a class="font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" href="http://www.promo.net/pg/">Project Gutenberg</a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">The recipients of the $8,000 "win" from RC5-56, Project Gutenberg's mission in life is to transcribe all the classics of literature to machine-readable form and release them freely for public use. Download a good book today!</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3">
          <a class="font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" href="http://www.eff.org/">Electronic Frontier Foundation</a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">The Electronic Frontier Foundation is a non-profit civil liberties organization working in the public interest to protect privacy, free expression, and access to public resources and information online, as well as to promote responsibility in new media.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3">
          <a class="font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" href="http://www.fsf.org/">Free Software Foundation</a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">The Free Software Foundation (FSF) is dedicated to eliminating restrictions on copying, redistribution, understanding, and modification of computer programs. They do this by promoting the development and use of free software in all areas of computing---but most particularly, by helping to develop the GNU operating system</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3">
          <a class="font-semibold text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" href="http://www.distributed.net/">distributed.net</a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">distributed.net (or more accurately Distributed Computing Technologies, Inc) is a non-profit venture whose sole focus is to test the limits of distributed computing and quantify the power that can be harnessed by applying the concepts of distributed computing to consumer hardware.</p>
        </div>
